<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <%
    const landingHubJsonLd = {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What makes a car dealership landing page convert?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Identifying the vehicle before asking for anything else, keeping the form short, and giving the visitor one clear action. A landing page that makes someone type out their car's details from scratch loses people; one that recognises the car and asks them to confirm it feels far less like work."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Which landing page flow should I use for my market?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "If your country has an accessible vehicle registry API, a lookup flow gives the strongest conversion — the UK's DVLA is free, and the US equivalent (VIN decoding via NHTSA) is also free, though it needs a VIN rather than a plate. If no such lookup is worth building yet, guided form fields are the safe universal default. A single call-to-action suits traffic you'd rather close over the phone than capture in writing."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is a vehicle registry lookup available outside the UK?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It depends on the country. The UK's DVLA Vehicle Enquiry Service is free and public. The US has no free plate-lookup equivalent, but the NHTSA's VIN decoder is free and public if the visitor has their VIN to hand. Other markets vary — where no free option exists, guided form fields are the practical starting point."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I switch flows later, or combine them?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. A common approach is to lead with a lookup where one is available and fall back to guided form fields automatically if the vehicle isn't found — which is exactly how the UK implementation already behaves for unmatched plates."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Why build a separate landing page for each make and model?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A page written for \"sell your Porsche 911\" ranks and converts better than one generic \"sell your car\" page, because the copy, guide content and FAQ all speak directly to that model rather than to cars in general — both for search and for the visitor reading it. This applies whichever capture flow the page uses."
          }
        }
      ]
    };
  %>
  <%- include('partials/seo-head', {
    title: 'Car Dealership Landing Pages | Auto Galleria',
    description: 'Landing page flows for car dealerships and vehicle sellers — registry lookup, guided form fields, or a single call-to-action. Pick the flow that fits your market.',
    jsonLd: landingHubJsonLd
  }) %>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/tailwind.css" />
</head>
<body class="bg-slate-50 text-slate-800">

  <%- include('partials/navbar-brochure') %>

  <section class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-linear-to-br from-slate-900 via-blue-900 to-slate-800"></div>
    <div class="absolute -top-24 -left-16 h-64 w-64 rounded-full bg-blue-500/30 blur-3xl"></div>
    <div class="absolute -bottom-24 right-0 h-72 w-72 rounded-full bg-cyan-400/20 blur-3xl"></div>

    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 pt-28 pb-16 text-white sm:px-6 sm:pt-32 sm:pb-20 lg:px-8">
      <p class="section-eyebrow text-blue-200">Website components</p>
      <h1 class="max-w-3xl text-4xl font-bold leading-tight sm:text-5xl">Landing pages for car dealerships and vehicle sellers.</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg text-slate-200">Not every market has a free vehicle registry lookup like the UK's DVLA. Here are three ways to capture the enquiry — pick the one that fits what's available to you, and how much friction your traffic can take.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <main id="main-content" class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 md:py-16 lg:px-8">

    <div class="mx-auto mb-10 max-w-3xl text-center">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Three ways to capture the lead</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900">Same goal, different amount of friction</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">Each flow identifies what's being sold and gets a name and contact detail — the difference is how much work that takes, and what it costs to build.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">

      <div class="card card-hover flex flex-col">
        <div class="relative min-h-48 overflow-hidden bg-linear-to-br from-slate-800 via-slate-900 to-black p-7" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/40"></div>
          <div class="relative">
            <p class="text-center text-xl font-bold leading-tight text-white drop-shadow-lg">Sell Your <span class="text-cyan-400">Porsche 911</span></p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-center text-xs text-slate-300">Enter your registration number</p>
            <div class="relative mt-5">
              <div class="w-full rounded-xl border-2 border-white/30 bg-white/10 px-4 py-3 text-center text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-white backdrop-blur">AB12 ABC</div>
              <div class="absolute right-1.5 top-1/2 flex h-8 w-8 -translate-y-1/2 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-linear-to-br from-blue-500 to-cyan-500 text-sm text-white">&rarr;</div>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3 text-center text-[11px] text-slate-400">Secure lookup &middot; no data stored or shared</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col gap-2.5 p-5">
          <span class="inline-flex w-fit items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full bg-blue-50 px-2.5 py-1 text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-blue-700">Automated</span>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Registry lookup</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">One field. The plate or VIN is checked against a vehicle registry and the make, model and year come back automatically — the visitor confirms rather than types.</p>
          <p class="mt-auto border-t border-slate-100 pt-2.5 text-xs text-slate-500"><b class="font-semibold text-slate-700">Best for</b> — markets with an accessible registry API, like the UK's DVLA or US VIN decoding.</p>
          <a href="/components/landing-pages-dvla" class="mt-1 inline-flex w-fit items-center gap-1 text-sm font-semibold text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700">See the full UK implementation &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card card-hover flex flex-col">
        <div class="relative min-h-48 overflow-hidden bg-linear-to-br from-slate-800 via-slate-900 to-black p-7" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/40"></div>
          <div class="relative space-y-2.5">
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-2">
              <div class="rounded-xl border-2 border-white/30 bg-white/10 px-3 py-2.5 text-xs text-slate-300 backdrop-blur">Year &#9662;</div>
              <div class="rounded-xl border-2 border-white/30 bg-white/10 px-3 py-2.5 text-xs text-slate-300 backdrop-blur">Make &#9662;</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border-2 border-white/30 bg-white/10 px-3.5 py-2.5 text-xs text-slate-300 backdrop-blur">Model &#9662;</div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border-2 border-white/30 bg-white/10 px-3.5 py-2.5 text-sm text-slate-400 backdrop-blur">Jane Smith</div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border-2 border-white/30 bg-white/10 px-3.5 py-2.5 text-sm text-slate-400 backdrop-blur">jane@example.com</div>
            <div class="rounded-xl bg-linear-to-r from-blue-600 to-cyan-500 py-2.5 text-center text-sm font-bold text-white shadow-lg">Get My Offer</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col gap-2.5 p-5">
          <span class="inline-flex w-fit items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-50 px-2.5 py-1 text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-emerald-700">Universal</span>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Guided form fields</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Year, make and model as simple dropdowns or free-text fields, alongside name and contact details. No external API, so it works in any market from day one.</p>
          <p class="mt-auto border-t border-slate-100 pt-2.5 text-xs text-slate-500"><b class="font-semibold text-slate-700">Best for</b> — a new market, or anywhere a lookup isn't worth building yet.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card card-hover flex flex-col">
        <div class="relative flex min-h-48 flex-col items-center justify-center overflow-hidden bg-linear-to-br from-slate-800 via-slate-900 to-black p-7 text-center" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/40"></div>
          <div class="relative">
            <p class="text-lg font-bold text-white drop-shadow-lg">Sell Your Car Today</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-slate-300">No forms. Just a quick chat.</p>
            <div class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-linear-to-r from-blue-600 to-cyan-500 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-white shadow-lg">
              <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13.601 2.326A7.96 7.96 0 0 0 8.003 0C3.58 0 .035 3.54.035 7.907c0 1.394.372 2.75 1.076 3.94L0 16l4.263-1.106a8.047 8.047 0 0 0 3.74.949h.003c4.422 0 7.968-3.539 7.968-7.906a7.868 7.868 0 0 0-2.373-5.611Z"/></svg>
              Chat on WhatsApp
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col gap-2.5 p-5">
          <span class="inline-flex w-fit items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full bg-amber-50 px-2.5 py-1 text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-amber-700">Lowest friction</span>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Single call-to-action</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">One button leading straight to a call or chat, rather than a form at all. Best when the goal is a conversation, not written data.</p>
          <p class="mt-auto border-t border-slate-100 pt-2.5 text-xs text-slate-500"><b class="font-semibold text-slate-700">Best for</b> — paid mobile traffic, or a seller who'd rather close over the phone.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto mb-8 mt-16 max-w-3xl text-center">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Common questions</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900">Landing pages, answered</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-4">
      <% landingHubJsonLd.mainEntity.forEach(faq => { %>
        <details class="rounded-lg bg-white p-4 shadow-sm">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-slate-800"><%= faq.name %></summary>
          <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600"><%= faq.acceptedAnswer.text %></p>
        </details>
      <% }) %>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-16 rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 text-center shadow-sm sm:p-10">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Ready when you are</p>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 sm:text-3xl">Want a landing page built for your market?</h2>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-3 max-w-xl text-slate-600">We'll help you pick the right flow and set up the lead capture, guide content and FAQ for your make and model.</p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col justify-center gap-3 sm:flex-row">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">Start a conversation</a>
        <a href="/components/landing-pages-dvla" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-slate-700 transition hover:bg-slate-50">See the UK registry-lookup version</a>
      </div>
    </div>

  </main>

  <%- include('partials/footer-brochure') %>

</body>
</html>
